-- ¶3: the day of signing.
@ref akn:preamble/p3
`the 1998 provident-fund agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 12 1998

-- ¶13: in the collective agreement of 8.9.98 the parties agreed that from
-- 1.1.98 contributions are made to a provident fund (its §10, imported).
@ref akn:preamble/p13
`the undertaking the 1998 provident-fund agreement carries out` MEANS `the cost of the employer's provident-fund share under the 1998 Oz agreement`

§§ `1–4 מבוא, תחולה וקופת הגמל`

-- akn:art_2 The heading of §2.

@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_1/p1
`the 1998 provident-fund agreement's preamble is part of it` MEANS TRUE

-- §2(א): every employee in the teaching scale whom the organisation
-- represents ("עובדי הוראה"). (ב): for the avoidance of doubt, no
-- contribution for the time a teacher spends in a sabbatical, save for the
-- teaching he in fact does while in it.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a
GIVEN `in the teaching scale` IS A BOOLEAN, `represented by the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1998 provident-fund agreement applies to` `in the teaching scale` `represented by the organisation` IF
    `the 1998 Oz agreement applies to` `in the teaching scale` `represented by the organisation`

@ref akn:art_2__para_b
GIVEN `in a sabbatical` IS A BOOLEAN, `teaching in fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc in the month
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a month carries provident-fund contributions under the 1998 agreement` `in a sabbatical` `teaching in fact` IF
    (NOT `in a sabbatical`) OR `teaching in fact`

-- (ג): the government acts to apply it to the teachers of the "owners",
-- whom it supervises and funds.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c
`applying the provident-fund agreement to the owners' teachers` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `act to apply the provident-fund agreement to the owners' teaching employees`

-- §3: this agreement is an inseparable annex of the agreement of 8.9.98.
@ref akn:art_3 akn:art_3/p1
`the 1998 provident-fund agreement is an annex of the agreement of 8.9.98` MEANS TRUE

-- §4: a provident fund here is a provident fund for employees' benefits
-- ("קופת גמל לתגמולים לשכירים") under the Income Tax (Rules for Approving
-- and Running Provident Funds) Regulations, 5724-1964 (outside the
-- corpus): a fund that does not pay an annuity. The organisation chooses
-- the teachers' fund, with the wages commissioner's written consent.
@ref akn:art_4 akn:art_4/p1
DECLARE `kind of fund the 1998 provident-fund agreement pays into` IS ONE OF
    `a provident fund for employees' benefits`
    `a pension fund`

`the fund the 1998 provident-fund agreement pays into` MEANS `a provident fund for employees' benefits`

`choosing the teachers' provident fund` MEANS
    PARTY `the secondary teachers' organisation`
    MUST  `choose the teachers' provident fund`
    HENCE (PARTY `the wages commissioner at the Treasury`
           MAY   `consent in writing to the organisation's choice of fund`)

§§ `5 ההפרשה`

-- The opening: from 1.1.98 the employers transfer to the fund, for every
-- employee the agreement covers, as follows.
-- (א): from 1.1.1998 the employer contributes 5% every month and deducts 5%
-- from the employee every month, on the salary components and other
-- payments the employer pays that are not pensionable and carry no
-- contribution to the Dafna fund, save the tax gross-up and the benefit
-- imputed for tax, and save any reward paid for out-of-school activity
-- (which §4.ו of the agreement of 8.9.98 also keeps out). (ב): for the
-- avoidance of doubt, nothing is contributed on the jubilee grant and the
-- clothing allowance of employees on a budgetary pension.
@ref akn:art_5 akn:art_5/p1 akn:art_5__para_a akn:art_5__para_b
`the employer's provident-fund contribution under the 1998 agreement` MEANS 5%
`the employee's provident-fund deduction under the 1998 agreement` MEANS 5%

DECLARE `payment the 1998 provident-fund agreement tells apart` IS ONE OF
    `a pensionable payment`
    `a payment carrying Dafna contributions`
    `a tax gross-up payment`
    `a benefit imputed for tax payment`
    `a reward for out-of-school activity`
    `the jubilee grant`
    `the clothing allowance payment`
    `an expense reimbursement payment`
    `another payment that is not pensionable`

DECLARE `pension of the 1998 provident-fund agreement's teacher` IS ONE OF
    `a budgetary pension`
    `an accrual pension`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      p IS A `payment the 1998 provident-fund agreement tells apart`
      k IS A `pension of the 1998 provident-fund agreement's teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1998 provident-fund agreement contributes on` d p k IF
        d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1998)
    AND NOT p EQUALS `a pensionable payment`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `a payment carrying Dafna contributions`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `a tax gross-up payment`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `a benefit imputed for tax payment`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `a reward for out-of-school activity`
    AND NOT (    k EQUALS `a budgetary pension`
             AND (p EQUALS `the jubilee grant` OR p EQUALS `the clothing allowance payment`))

-- The contribution and the deduction on a payment of a month: 5% and 5%,
-- where (א) brings the payment in; NOTHING where it does not.
@desc The provident-fund contribution and deduction on a payment, under the agreement of 17.12.98.
DECLARE `1998 provident-fund amounts` HAS
    `the employer's contribution` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's deduction`    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      p IS A `payment the 1998 provident-fund agreement tells apart`
      k IS A `pension of the 1998 provident-fund agreement's teacher`
      amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `1998 provident-fund amounts`
DECIDE `the 1998 provident-fund amounts on` d p k amount IS
    IF `the 1998 provident-fund agreement contributes on` d p k
    THEN JUST (`1998 provident-fund amounts` WITH
                  `the employer's contribution` IS `the employer's provident-fund contribution under the 1998 agreement` TIMES amount
                  `the employee's deduction`    IS `the employee's provident-fund deduction under the 1998 agreement` TIMES amount)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (ג): the retroactive contribution, for every month from 1.1.98 to the
-- start of contributing in fact, is made in December 1998, and only after
-- the fund is chosen under §4 — in writing, by 17.12.98 at the latest, by
-- the Income Tax Commission's approval.
@ref akn:art_5__para_c
`the last day to choose the fund` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 12 1998

`making the retroactive contribution` MEANS
    PARTY `the secondary teachers' organisation`
    MUST  `choose the teachers' provident fund`
    WITHIN DATE_SERIAL `the last day to choose the fund` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the 1998 provident-fund agreement was signed on`
    HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `make the retroactive provident-fund contribution`
           WITHIN DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 1998) MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the last day to choose the fund`)

-- (ד): from the start in fact the contribution is made every month; the
-- Wage Protection Law, 1958, applies to it (outside the corpus).
@ref akn:art_5__para_d
`transferring the monthly contribution` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `transfer the provident-fund contributions`

`why the Wage Protection Law is not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק הגנת השכר, התשי\"ח-1958"

-- (ה): a teacher in a sabbatical in תשנ"ח has the retroactive contribution
-- only for the months he in fact taught. (ו): a teacher who taught in
-- תשנ"ח and is in a sabbatical in תשנ"ט has the retroactive contribution,
-- the employee's share too, made by the employer only for the months he
-- taught in תשנ"ח from 1.1.98; he reimburses the employer for his share as
-- soon as he is asked; if not by the end of תשנ"ט (31.8.1999), the sum is
-- deducted from his first salary on his return to teaching.
@ref akn:art_5__para_e akn:art_5__para_f
GIVEN `months from 1.1.98 he in fact taught in 5758` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the months of the retroactive contribution in a sabbatical case` `months from 1.1.98 he in fact taught in 5758` IS
    `months from 1.1.98 he in fact taught in 5758`

GIVEN `reimbursed by the end of 5759` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `1998 provident-fund agreement action`
DECIDE `the sabbatical teacher's share of the retroactive contribution` `reimbursed by the end of 5759` IS
    IF `reimbursed by the end of 5759`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `deduct the employee's share from the first salary on return`

§§ `6–8 זכויות העובד, כפל הפרשה ותקדים`

-- akn:art_6 The heading of §6.
-- akn:art_7 The heading of §7.
-- akn:art_8 The heading of §8.

-- §6: every employee has, when the employment ends and in every other case
-- usual for a provident fund, all the sums gathered for him in the fund,
-- on the terms that entitle to benefits under the regulations of 1964
-- (outside the corpus).
@ref akn:art_6/p1
`the employee is entitled to all the sums gathered in the fund` MEANS TRUE

-- §7: for a teacher for whom contributions to a pension or a provident fund
-- are made on a component, not under this agreement, while they are made,
-- none is made on that component under it: never twice.
@ref akn:art_7/p1
GIVEN `contributions are made on it not under this agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would be brought in under §5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1998 provident-fund agreement contributes on the component` `contributions are made on it not under this agreement` `would be brought in under §5` IF
    `would be brought in under §5` AND (NOT `contributions are made on it not under this agreement`)

-- §8: the agreement on its own teaches no duty to contribute on these
-- components to other funds, training funds among them, nor to count them
-- for severance pay or the hour value, and recognises none of them for a
-- pension by law.
@ref akn:art_8/p1
DECLARE `what §8 says the 1998 components do not thereby count for` IS ONE OF
    `other funds, training funds among them`
    `severance pay`
    `the hour value`
    `a pension by law`

GIVEN p IS A `what §8 says the 1998 components do not thereby count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1998 provident-fund agreement on its own makes the components count for` p IF FALSE

§§ `9 מעבר להפרשות לפנסיה`

-- akn:art_9 The heading of §9, a number with no title.

-- (א): from the stage at which pension contributions are made for the
-- engineers on a budgetary pension in the State's service on any of the
-- components that are not pensionable, in place of the provident fund
-- (save for expense reimbursements), contributions and deductions are made
-- for teachers insured in a budgetary or an accrual pension too — on
-- condition that the whole cost of contributions on those components, to
-- the provident fund and to an accrual pension fund if so agreed, is no
-- more than the employers' share §10 of the agreement of 8.9.98 sets
-- (0.8% of the salary determining the pension, imported). (ב): carrying
-- out (א) needs a new agreement between the parties and another with the
-- pension fund ("the pension agreements"). (ג): the employer's undertakings
-- under the pension agreements, to the pension fund and to the provident
-- fund for expense reimbursements, take the place of those under this one,
-- within (א)'s cost.
@ref akn:art_9__para_a akn:art_9__para_b akn:art_9__para_c
GIVEN `pension contributions made for the State's engineers on such components` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pension agreements were made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost as a share of the pension salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pension agreements take the place of the 1998 provident-fund agreement` `pension contributions made for the State's engineers on such components` `the pension agreements were made` `the cost as a share of the pension salary` IF
        `pension contributions made for the State's engineers on such components`
    AND `the pension agreements were made`
    AND `the cost as a share of the pension salary` AT MOST `the cost of the employer's provident-fund share under the 1998 Oz agreement`

`making the pension agreements` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `make the new pension agreements`

§§ `10 גימלאים`

-- akn:art_10 The heading of §10, a number with no title.

-- Notwithstanding §9, for the teachers who retired from 1.1.98 to 30.11.98
-- no contribution is made under this agreement: they are paid once the
-- sum of the employer's contributions under it for every month from 1.1.98
-- to their retirement, from 1.2.99 and by 1.3.99 at the latest. (The rule
-- it sets aside is §5's retroactive contribution; the section names §9.)
@ref akn:art_10/p1
GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 1998 retiree is paid a one-time sum in place of contributions` `retired on` IF
        `retired on` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1998)
    AND `retired on` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 1998)

GIVEN `the employer's monthly contributions until retirement` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1998 retiree's one-time sum` `the employer's monthly contributions until retirement` IS
    sum `the employer's monthly contributions until retirement`

`paying the retired teacher's one-time sum` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the retired teacher's one-time sum`
    WITHIN DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 1999) MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the 1998 provident-fund agreement was signed on`

`the 1998 retiree's one-time sum is paid from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 1999

